+## Review `review-60f652c3e40fcdc9`
+
+Repaired the retained union-versus-XOR teaching defect on generator version
+2.1.0 (`7a50a0aa...`). The old consecutive lesson at seed 0, medium, demos
+1–4 had no shared red/blue anchored offsets, so a union shortcut fit every
+demonstration and failed only on query 5.
+
+Version 2.2.0 schedules an overlap witness at every sample index divisible by
+`EXAMPLES_NEEDED` (4). Every four consecutive integer indices therefore contain
+one such witness. Scheduled witnesses also require the full union footprint to
+be in bounds and empty at the cyan target, so the cancellation is visibly
+label-distinguishing rather than clipped or overwritten.
+
+Added:
+
+- an independent Python mirror of the canonical anchored-XOR rule;
+- an executable clipped-union lesson competitor;
+- `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS`, `LESSON_COMPETITORS`, and `lesson_identifiable`;
+- focused regression tests covering the historical lesson, consecutive-window
+  coverage across all three bands, and executable rival disagreement;
+- reusable `workspace/check_union_lesson.py` for bounded Racket-backed replay.
+
+Verification:
+
+- 3/3 portable task tests pass;
+- six lessons (easy/medium/hard × seeds 0 and 17), 30 direct generated inputs,
+  and 30 public Racket labels pass;
+- every checked lesson has an overlap demonstration, refutes union from the
+  demonstrations alone, passes the lesson gate, and matches the independent XOR
+  mirror.
+
+The retained check is finite; it does not prove uniqueness against arbitrary
+rules or all seeds. The production canonical Racket rule is unchanged.
